                <pb facs="0659" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg647"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/279: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Burdett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-06T19:00:00-03:00">December 6, 1940—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 6—6:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>639. Reference Embassy’s telegram No. 636, December 6, 3 p.m. The Rio press today
                    published interviews with the Argentine and Chilean Ambassadors and the
                    Dominican Minister here each warmly supporting the Brazilian case in the recent
                    maritime incidents.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Burdett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
